The '''Levante''' ({{IPA|bl|leˈβante|lang}}; {{Langx|mxi|لِيبَانْتِي|Libánti}}; {{Literal translation|the place of rising|the east}}), also known as the '''Aethiopic Coast''', is a name used to refer to the territory of Balisca that lies east of the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]], on than the [[Abyala|Abyalan]] [[Aethiopian Ocean|Aethiopian]] coast. It roughly corresponds to the former area under the influence of the [[Hesperian League]], but has no modern geopolitical definition. Rather, it broadly includes the communities of [[Hesperia]] (all regions except [[Trás-as-Montanyas]]), Aethiopic [[Araucaria]] ([[Luzamontaña]], [[Juyú]] and [[Brasal]]), and sometimes the [[Castejón Metropolis]].

Among inhabitants of the Levante, the term is rarely used. Its literal meaning is "the east", and thus makes sense only from the perspective of those who live to the west of the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]].

